<title>SPAIN: Spain Q2 GDP rises 1.9 pct vs Q2 1995.</title>
<headline>Spain Q2 GDP rises 1.9 pct vs Q2 1995.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute gave the following figures, in 1986 prices (pctg change):</p>
<p> GROSS DOMESTIC PRODUCT	   Q2 '96   Q1 '96   Q2 96 VS Q1 96</p>
<p>					  yr/yr     yr/yr    qtr/qtr</p>
<p> Gross domestic product	    +1.9     +2.0	+0.5</p>
<p> Private consumption		 +1.9     +1.7	+0.6</p>
<p> Public sector consumption	   0.6     1.0     0.0</p>
<p> Gross fixed capital formation     1.6     3.1     0.4</p>
<p>    Capital goods			6.4     5.6     2.1</p>
<p>    Construction			-1.0     1.7    -0.6</p>
<p> Variation in stocks		   0.2     0.2     N/A</p>
<p> Internal demand			 1.8     2.1     0.5</p>
<p> Exports				   9.1     8.7     1.9</p>
<p> Imports				   8.2     8.4     1.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Q1 figures for 1996 are revised.</p>
<p>INE also revised down GDP growth during the fourth quarter of 1995 to 2.2 percent year on year from a previous figure of 2.3 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
